Diagnostics for "how wide is this batch actually running?"

The wave selector is provably correct - a 20-episode batch with two subtitles per episode on a
single disk selects four jobs, and eight when eight workers are configured (harness covers both)
- so a batch that runs two at a time is either configured that way or held fewer eligible tasks
than expected. Both are now visible instead of guessed:

- the batch view reports the effective worker limit, and the run line shows "2/4 workers"
  (running / limit) whenever the batch is parallel and has work left;
- every wave logs its width: "Wave: starting 2 job(s) (worker limit 4, mode ultimate, 37 still
  queued) for batch ...".

Harness: 90 checks, ALL PASS, including the 20-episode cases.

Version 1.1.0.26.
